+   "body": "Arthur,\n\nThe Zombie Match 3D Season Pass transfer register is done and shared with you as reader (no cc, no attachment, no public or domain-wide link).\n\nRegister: https://drive.google.com/file/d/ce4d7ce23d8d68cb/view\nFile: Season Pass transfer register.csv, in the engineering transfer folder.\n\nEvidence snapshot: 12 February 2026, 18:00 UTC, per the amendment on the Season Pass scope control card. Delivering now rather than waiting for the review hold.\n\nClass totals over the 128 in-scope components (cohort matrix, game = Zombie Match 3D and Transfer = include):\n  READY 50\n  WATCH 10\n  HOLD  68\n  Total 128\n\nHOLD blockers by failed condition (a component is counted under every condition it fails, so these sum to more than 68):\n  failed assertions above zero - 28\n  test artifact different from receipt artifact - 4\n  selected transfer review not APPROVED for the receipt artifact - 28\n  billing hold active at snapshot - 15\n  missing input - 5\n\nHistorical event comparison, kept separate from the component counts: 6 completed Zombie Match 3D Season Pass live-ops events with an end date on or before 12 February 2026, 754 participants in total. That is historical context only, not a count of engineering components.\n\nHow the evidence was selected, for the record:\n- Receipts: replayed each PR's own-package release journal by effective_at through the snapshot. Withdrawals clear the pointer with no automatic fallback, a rollback only restores an earlier issued, non-withdrawn receipt, and copies never restore validity. Five components have no current receipt at the snapshot and are recorded as missing input rather than falling back to a withdrawn upload.\n- Receipts pasted onto the wrong package were ignored, as you confirmed in the thread; each component uses its own PR's receipt.\n- Validation: for lineage-bound receipts, runs were taken from the fixture named by the active receipt, latest completed entitlement run per required platform; split mode sums ios and android. Diagnostic, smoke, aborted and incomplete runs were treated as ineligible and do not erase the last qualifying result.\n- Reviews: lane=source reviews were excluded. Where the active receipt carries an acceptance epoch, the review was taken from that epoch only; a later review in a different epoch was not substituted even where its digest matched. For dismissed epoch-bound reviews the snapshot state was reconstructed from the submitted decision and the dated dismissal, so a dismissal after the snapshot leaves the submitted decision in force.\n- Billing hold was reconstructed from the PR label timeline at the snapshot, not from current labels.\n\nThe review deck's Handoff status slide and tracking issue ZOM-801 are updated to match, and ZOM-801 is now In Validation. Validation issues and all PRs were left untouched. This is the evidence review packet, not an approval to ship.\n\nOliver\n"
